    {
      "id": "claim_c720f70c625348579dd00a294a7552df",
      "statement": "Authenticator status updates (authorization URL, device code, waiting messages) are always plain human-readable text written to stderr via the injected Status callback regardless of the command's output mode, and OCM auth failures deliberately avoid wrapping the underlying OAuth error because oauth2.RetrieveError can carry a raw token-endpoint response body; ocmAuthError instead classifies failures into a small fixed reason set (canceled, expired, denied, invalid_response, network, other).",
